{
    "method": "customerAnalytics.accountRelationshipDefinitionsList",
    "toolName": "account-relationship-definitions-list",
    "operationId": "account_relationship_definitions_list",
    "title": "List account relationship definitions",
    "category": "Customer analytics",
    "description": "List Customer Analytics account relationship definitions for the project. A definition is a team-defined relationship type between a PostHog user and an account (e.g. CSM, Onboarding manager) with a `name`, optional `description`, and `is_single_holder` flag (whether only one user can hold it per account at a time). Definitions are team-scoped and shared across all accounts; the users assigned to a specific account are managed via the account relationship tools. To query definitions in bulk, HogQL `system.account_relationship_definitions` covers the same data. When a request names an account role, check this project's definitions before assuming it is a relationship. For a named teammate, search `org-members-list` by email and confirm the returned `user.email` equals the requested email, ignoring case, before using the user id to query active assignments.",
